; Set bounds on the *compact* `:names [a b c]` spelling. Legal, and
; deliberately so: the aggregate needs no per-head metadata, and "exactly
; one of these four" is the common case — forcing it to spell every head
; as a `(head …)` child would be a tax on the shape the feature is for.
;
; It is also what invalidated the old promise that a compact head-set is
; always unbounded. Nothing here declares a per-head bound, so if the
; count sweep still keyed on that alone, both forms below would validate
; clean.
;
; `(data …)` is the second WebGPU-adjacent shape the ask filed: at most
; one generator, none being fine. That is `:max-children 1` with no
; floor — which the per-head spelling can express only as "at most one
; cube AND at most one sphere", satisfied by one of each.
(plugin :name pngine :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name data-shape-section
    :description "The one generator a (data …) may carry."
    :underlying form
    :heads (head-set :names [cube sphere teapot] :max-children 1))

  (form :name cube
    (key :name size :type number))
  (form :name sphere
    (key :name radius :type number))
  (form :name teapot)

  (form :name data
    :positional data-shape-section
    (key :name name :type symbol)))

; No generator: fine, the set declares no floor.
(data :name empty)
; One generator: fine.
(data :name solid (cube :size 2))
; Two: over the set's ceiling, though each head is well within its own
; (absent) bound.
(data :name both (cube :size 2) (sphere :radius 1))
